    {
      "tag": "Stop 1",
      "h2": "Law vs norm",
      "body_html": "<p class=\"big\">A <span class=\"hl p\">crime</span> breaks the <b>law</b> — written rules with state-set punishments.</p><p><span class=\"hl p\">Deviance</span> breaks a <b>norm</b> — unwritten expectations like queueing politely.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 2",
      "h2": "Same act, different label",
      "body_html": "<p>What's a crime depends on time and place:</p><ul><li>Cannabis legal in some US states, illegal in UK.</li><li>Drinking at 16 was once normal, now restricted.</li><li>Slavery was legal long ago — now a global crime.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 3",
      "h2": "Sanctions",
      "body_html": "<p><span class=\"hl y\">Sanctions</span> = social responses.</p><ul><li><b>Positive</b> — praise, awards.</li><li><b>Negative</b> — fine, jail, exclusion.</li></ul><p>Society uses sanctions to keep order. 🚓</p>"
    }
  ],
